# Enterprise Creator Intelligence (Frozen · Maintenance Mode)

**Status:** **FROZEN · Maintenance Mode · COMPLETE** (Release 2.3 Phase 1)  
**Acceptance:** `docs/architecture/ENTERPRISE_CREATOR_INTELLIGENCE_ACCEPTANCE.md`  
**Spec:** `docs/architecture/ENTERPRISE_CREATOR_INTELLIGENCE.md`  
**Code:** `lib/enterprise-creator-intelligence/`  
**Registry:** `docs/architecture/PLATFORM_CAPABILITY_REGISTRY.md`  
**Canonical entry:** `loadCreatorIntelligenceBundle` / `loadCreatorIntelligenceBundles`

## Mandatory

1. Planning · Client · Campaign · Reporting · Analytics · AI · Mobile **must** consume Creator Intelligence **only** via `@/lib/enterprise-creator-intelligence` (`loadCreatorIntelligenceBundle`).
2. Do **not** invent parallel creator investment scores, audience-quality investment signals, or commercial/performance/category intelligence engines for those consumers.
3. Discovery Thinkway Score (`lib/creators/thinkway-score.ts`) and campaign-decision simulation scores are **not** Enterprise Creator Intelligence — Discovery/simulation only.
4. Sprint 1–6 baselines are protected — extend, do not redesign.
5. Append-only history only — never overwrite prior intelligence captures.
6. Shared cache (`createEciFactsCache`) prevents recomputation — never changes calculations.
7. Every layer exposes **Confidence** and **Evidence Coverage**; confidence must not exceed evidence coverage.
8. AI-ready hints only — **no AI execution** unless a later approved initiative.
9. No Production deploy of ECI schema without explicit approval.

## Maintenance Mode only

- Defect / type / build fixes  
- Performance / caching improvements that do not change calculation semantics  
- Sibling extensions (Brand Safety, Fraud, Pricing Prediction, etc.) that **extend** the package  

## Forbidden

- Redesign of Historical / Commercial / Category / Performance / Audience / Investment layer contracts  
- Parallel investment recommendation engines  
- Using Discovery scores as Planning investment SSOT  

## Active initiative after freeze

**Planning Workspace** may begin — must consume `loadCreatorIntelligenceBundle`.

